{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld","id":1472918,"title":"Vampire Otherworld","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-20T19:24:09-08:00","id":1472918,"title":"Vampire Otherworld","content":"I saw a brief mention in the 3rd ed. wish list about the possibility of a distinctly Kindred otherworld, something separate from the Underworld, which is a concept I've been eager to see ever since the transition from World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I'm curious if The forum has any canon, any informed speculation, or any news on the idea before I play around fleshing out the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T19:57:00-08:00","id":1472919,"title":"","content":"The thing to know about Vampire is that it's kind of opposite Mage in terms of cosmological niche in a lot of ways; Deviant has presented a closer analogue, and Hunter's been adjacent to the line pretty much since 1.5e started rolling out the clanbooks and Ancient Mysteries with conspiracy cameos in them.<br /> <br /> Mages are the supernatural one-percent, and academics besides; the nature of their power and insight encourages them to delve into occult minutiae and retreat from mortal society, and they can spend their years exploring any of the myriad otherworlds present in the setting apart from the ones that obliterate any visitors who haven't got divine power or aid holding them together, albeit some of those worlds have inhabitants that are exceedingly dangerous to beings of mortal constitution. Werewolves, changelings, and Sin-Eaters have a metaphysical tie to specific segments of the cosmology and often have specific reasons to make use of that tie. Beasts have the ability to leverage existing passageways to most other worlds, but the way their powerset works means extended sojourns in those environments will wear badly on them or their relationships, and most of them spend more time dealing with prosaic concerns in the waking world than meddling in the Astral for the same reason.<br /> <br /> Deviants are a bunch of different things with a few shared qualities, and they don't go poking around deep in other dimensions for much the same reason Beasts don't with the volume knob turned up. The closest thing demons have to a unified otherworld is a very slightly more magical version of the thing that vampires have (see anon). Hunters are largely flying blind for thematic reasons that are well-established.<br /> <br /> Vampires are constantly starving and their primary advantages work on mortals and vampires who they have specific forms of leverage over; they're a bunch of different things with a few shared qualities acquired by extended proximity to and consumption of humanity (and each other); the aggregate of their shared metaphysical state absorbs qualities from their surroundings (including other supernatural qualities, especially curses), and the pursuit of directed magical evolution is typically characterized as a luxury available to characters who don't have to worry about where their next meal is coming from; the main way vampires increase the security of their feeding process is through good old institutional corruption and otherwise turning people and places into extensions of themselves, most easily through the inter-vampire social structures managed by Elysium and the covenants.<br /> <br /> The All Night Society is the distinctly Kindred otherworld. The Predatory Aura laying thick across a character's Feeding Grounds is the distinctly Kindred otherworld. Vampires and their mark upon the land are the distinctly Kindred otherworld. Everything else is an extra to squeeze for more power and comfort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T20:01:54-08:00","id":1472921,"title":"","content":"What Satchel said above, but maybe you could incorporate the Shadow from Trinity Continuum: Assassins if you want something even stranger (see the forums/main site for previews). Powered by the Predatory Aura and the Curse itself, of course, instead of Flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T18:19:42-08:00","id":1473014,"title":"","content":"Had a similar idea. In the end it turned out as something between Ravenloft setting and Bloodborne.<br /> A world in Lower Depths that lacks the concept of Death. Nothing ever dies.<br /> Add rivers of blood and viscera, fleshlands where meat is instead of dirt, where marrow grows like plants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-22T14:40:39-08:00","id":1473045,"title":"","content":"I think that the closest there is to a &quot;canon&quot; Vampire Otherworld is wherever the Strix come from- which is 99.9% some Lower Depth, but besides rare instances of Owls simply emerging or vanishing into that world and other such instances there is little in canon about this realm. Most fans simply call it Dis (due to the Strix being called &quot;Birds of Dis&quot; in RfR), but even the 2e book states that while the Strix may have came from another world, the vast majority of those have lived in the material for so damn long or are descended from generations of Owls which have never seen that original realm that they all basically consider the material as their &quot;native realm&quot;. So yeah, not much to work with, unless you want to imagine a whole world made out of smoke and shadows filled with bright golden eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T15:26:55-08:00","id":1473117,"title":"","content":"The closest thing I\u2019ve ever done to a vampire Otherworld is create the Vampiric Cloister known as Toburaishima- formerly an imperial Japanese colony out in the middle of nowhere in the pacific that was basically annexed by the US after WWII, turned into a naval base and a small vacation locale- its main attraction being near a blue hole that supposedly had a sunken structure resting at the bottom. <br /> <br /> What most didn\u2019t know is that the island was once home to a now long extinct clan of Kindred who were adept at suffusing their Blood into the world around them.. and it created a place that was very.. weird.. the island was almost like a vampire itself. Full of ancient secrets. And ghoulish ecosystems","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 01-23-2022, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T06:38:43-08:00","id":1473163,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be opposed to vampires having their own little slice of hell in the underworld, the fluff in geist even supports it but I wouldn't call it otherworld because I think that would just be a little &quot;dominion&quot; shall we say of the underworld where vamps are more likely to gather. I would be more interested as to how they would be able to access the underworld in the first place, aside from the conventional methods that are available to humans, there is a new bloodline in the new night horror book that allows more interaction with ghosts but still nothing that would help with unlocking an avernian gate.<br /> <br /> If you were thinking about an otherworld in the real world, I think that the all night society fit that niche perfectly, vampires are creatures inherently tied to the physical world, they need to otherwise they wouldn't be able to sustain themselves, no need to make a specific vampire superhaven when you have plenty of such places in practically every city in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 01-24-2022, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T09:08:26-08:00","id":1473170,"title":"","content":"Experimented a bit with the subject back in 1e, mostly expanding some concepts from <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/12201/Mythologies\" target=\"_blank\">Mythologies</a> by mixing with elements from Astral Realms, Book of Dead and others.<br /> <br /> From that blend of things came the idea of two levels of Torpor - the Sleep of Reason, the Surface or Oneiros Layer, that is the same as described in MtAw and Astral Realms (based on many telling similarities with the &quot;Understanding the Fog of Eternity&quot; subchapter from Mythologies) what means that through Torpor vampires can circumvent some of the requirements that Awakened deal with for astral journeys, up to the Oneiros at least, where some undead mystics have confronted what Mages might qualify as the soul's Daimon or entities akin to Goetic inner demons.<br /> <br /> \u200bBeyond that, things get a little turbid and less similar to what one of the awakened might expect from their &quot;inner dimensions&quot;, as below the impulses and urges of the Beast intrude and merge with the dark corners of a kindred identity past and present to form labyrinthine vistas at the same time alien and familiar to the dead predator once human that holds the ephemeral keys to the idiosyncratic landscape of these hedge mazes, endless caves of echoes and houses of phantasmagoric mirrors.<br /> <br /> And farther even lies only death - or more precisely, the place of the dead, the Thanatos Layer, the Second Death realm (again, as per Mythologies), a place of broken hungry dead without bodies and fetterless ghosts, many all too ready to steal the tether/silver cord of those visitors who still have it for a chance at new unlife in a repossessed body so to speak, even though the Psychocomps that guard that place strongly frown upon it and may attempt to find cracks into the world of the living to try to recapture such escapees with bodies not their own.<br /> <br /> That ain't everything, but is what i can remember without taking some time to look in a bunch of notes about a decade old, give or take. But overall one might say the kindred nature, like their vitae, would pool in places and then slip through cracks into different spaces, all the while coagulating upon them through their passage, blending both ends and the paths leading to and fro them into something more of the hungry dead and the ichors, mostly crimson and human but not always that fuels them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-24-2022, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T22:17:39-08:00","id":1473234,"title":"","content":"<i>Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead</i> has a story about a Founder who traveled to Dis (the place where the Strix went).<br /> <br /> <br /> Whenever I need to destabilize things in my game, someone gets access to Dis. <br /> <br /> This is what I have in my notes for when people end up in Dis. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u2014</span></span>a grey forest, lit by a grey directionless light. the trees are grey and twisted and dead. cremation ash ground<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u2014</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u2014</span></span>dark shapes in the distance. they are hungry<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u2014</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u2014</span></span>dark things above. crowding into the trees. Hateful hungry eyes staring down at you<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u2014</span></span><ul><li>Set up two progress tracks/clocks. One progresses towards escape, the other to confrontation.</li> <li>Traversal is an extended roll using the lower of (Humanity - BP) or (Resolve + Composure - BP).<ul><li>Success gets a short interactive nightmare/hallucination sequence with plot hints and advances the exit track.</li> <li>Failure gets hints about the Strix's nature (find a pre-human skull, the owls' eyes shine, etc), but the Strix get closer.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> If the Strix reach the PCs, they want blood/breath/a ride out of Dis, and they have knowledge and power to offer. Curious and they sense an opportunity; posture like they have the upper hand. They're set up so the players expect violence, but they won't attack until the PCs become an obstacle to their escaping.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T08:47:29-08:00","id":1473264,"title":"","content":"I think you could get something out of the idea that vampires have a capacity to immerse themselves more deeply in the things that Satchel pointed out, make the experience of them more literal for the vampire. My impromptu idea for how that would function for Requiem's themes is that the vampire gets to inhabit a rendering of the world where they feel less alienated (among which are elements where they don't need to feel so hostile towards one another), but it comes at the cost of connections to humanity. Not just in terms of being isolated from Touchstones and the experience itself causing Breaking Points, but that there isn't really anything to feed on in there.<br /> <br /> The horror could come from an element where a vampire in that state of being won't actually be driven into Torpor, but such a thing is cold comfort, as it just makes it a place of perpetual gnawing hunger. You'd expect most vampires to only ever skim the surface of it, but occasionally you find some horrors who'll take hunger and inhumanity as the fair price for a place where they can function more openly and feel as though they belong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T11:36:15-08:00","id":1473350,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> that concept gets bonus points from me for managing to make something cool out of Mythologies' obsolete material","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T20:52:55-08:00","id":1473378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1473350#post1473350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> that concept gets bonus points from me for managing to make something cool out of Mythologies' obsolete material</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks.<br /> <br /> Funny thing is that the maze of mirrors was the first otherworldly thing, along with Red Jack &amp; Blood Mary i threw in my chronicle, mostly straight from &quot;The Thing in the Mirror&quot; subchapter from Mythologies, with no clear idea of what i actually wanted them to be back then, if i'm being honest. But then comes the Mekhet clanbook with Hollows, what led to considerable streamlining and expansion of Jack's actual nature, identity and the motives behind the extensive network of pupils/additional anchors he has built, with the House That Jack Built (the Glass Mansion from Reliquary) at the center of it all.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Mary would stretch herself from mirrors into her own personal tract of the Hedge, taken from the Children of the Thorns in Danse Macabre and more focused in a complex multi-tiered conflict between mirrors, dreams &amp; beyond with the Sightless Mother (from Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners) and La Llorona (from Shadows of Mexico), involving the Children of Thorns, the Moirai, Alucinor, Usiri &amp; Cihuateteo (Wicked Dead and kindred versions both) among others.<br /> <br /> (Also, it's possible that Blood Mary is actually Pasiphae aka another version of the Sightless Mother)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-26-2022, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T20:14:46-08:00","id":1474834,"title":"","content":"So a long while ago I addressed this in my own game by making my own lost Clan called Alukah. I actually called this other place the Otherworld (I think, its been ages). For their proprietary Discipline I used an updated Blood Tenebrose (A mish mash of a few other peoples updated Blood Tenebrose with my own touches). The way I looked at it, this Kindred Clan was a bit of a Death Spirit, so they gained access in both the Shadow and Underworld. But, because Kindred are a paranoid lot who keep secrets, lore was sparse so the Clan for the most part wouldn't see a separating line between the Shadow/Underworld, they would just see it as different places in the Otherworld. The game being run was Cross-Line heavy, so it really worked. Plus I have a huge Soul Reaver bent, and while a Mekhet Bloodline could fill that role, I felt a new, more bizarre clan would suit better. I think the Alukah is still around here in the Homebrew section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T17:51:51-08:00","id":1475010,"title":"","content":"Building up on everything in the thread, I think it is worth to explore more in the books how vampires may corrupt things with their presence and/or actions, that being their &quot;otherworld&quot;. The Predatory Aura, the many curses in the blood and the passage of time may twist the places vampires stay in for too long, with Ghoul-like animals, plants and things following regardless of any actual effort or control by the vampire. Not only in the material world, but also in other worlds the undead touches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T20:20:36-08:00","id":1475016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1475010#post1475010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Building up on everything in the thread, I think it is worth to explore more in the books how vampires may corrupt things with their presence and/or actions, that being their &quot;otherworld&quot;. The Predatory Aura, the many curses in the blood and the passage of time may twist the places vampires stay in for too long, with Ghoul-like animals, plants and things following regardless of any actual effort or control by the vampire. Not only in the material world, but also in other worlds the undead touches.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very much so. The blood flows and trickles, making inroads out of cracks, spoiling &amp; washing away both things in its path, gathering all kinds of impurities within itself, new particles of good, bad and dead matter, feelings, life &amp; magic carried into the crimson flow of an unliving, undying circulatory system, for no greater reason than continued existence, that which motivates beasts of all kinds &amp; forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T16:47:46-08:00","id":1475269,"title":"","content":"Yeah that was essentially what was happening to Toburaishima. The vampiric Island had been been gradually changing for At least a thousand years and had become something.. different by the time of 2014, and was hinted to be about to undergo a metaphysical metamorphosis. I can only imagine what the island has become in 2022... having spent so long stewing in the Vitae of kindred both long extinct and those who came and went, attempting to mould it into their perfect kingdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 02-22-2022, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T11:42:38-07:00","id":1480381,"title":"","content":"On a rather humorous note, the Hunting Grounds share a lot of similarities with how I imagine Toburaishima to be, with a couple differences of course.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s very amusing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T12:54:49-07:00","id":1480389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1472921#post1472921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Satchel said above, but maybe you could incorporate the Shadow from Trinity Continuum: Assassins if you want something even stranger (see the forums/main site for previews). Powered by the Predatory Aura and the Curse itself, of course, instead of Flux.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s an interesting idea. Makes the Masquerade a lot more plausible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T12:22:08-07:00","id":1481105,"title":"","content":"One thing I played with a while back was having the beast represent attachment to a dark and twisted entity. This was sometimes believed to be a specific entity, but some question that and suggested that multiple forms represented the various aspects of the Curse. Others go so far as to say that each clan has their own patron. Some suggest all are part of something greater. Anyhow you slice it, though, these hungry blood gods live somewhere and that could be your otherworld.<br /> <br /> Vampires corrupting things (people, places) would be aligning them more closely to their otherworld. Especially dramatic corruption could lead to magical effects beyond the expected or even passage between realms.<br /> <br /> Even if this is true, most vampires wouldn't necessarily know it and factions would spring up that interpret the evidence very differently. One form might believe that consuming the souls of opposing clans would gain them favor. Others might seek to separate from these masters, in an effort to become something greater.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ed. To clarify: Vampires wouldn't work any differently just because of this; it's mostly a behind-the-scenes detail that can slip in, here and there.<br /> <br /> If there are competing blood gods out there, they might be vying for domination over the blood in the material realm. The striges might represent a jealous bloodline patron in conflict with the others or a thing that resents the existence of the realm..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 05-14-2022, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T00:13:24-07:00","id":1481166,"title":"","content":"Honestly I like the idea of the vampire otherworld being the realm of the Strix. Not only do kindred have practically no desire to go there, not only is it incredibly dangerous for them (because the Strix there will likely rip apart any who aren't of the Brood, and sone even them), but they can't even get there easily.<br /> <br /> Because in my personal canon the kindred aren't the 'true' or original vampires, the Strix are. Human-spirits locked away by mages at the dawn of mankind, they first tamed and then escaped their otherworld prison. The Strix can come and go relatively freely, even if few of them know how.<br /> <br /> Kindred here are the result of Strix using Synthesis back in the ancient times, and this created far more than eight types of vampire. But most of them got killed, either by humans or Strix, before having any descendants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T07:45:11-07:00","id":1481177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1481166#post1481166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I like the idea of the vampire otherworld being the realm of the Strix. Not only do kindred have practically no desire to go there, not only is it incredibly dangerous for them (because the Strix there will likely rip apart any who aren't of the Brood, and sone even them), but they can't even get there easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but things can be so much more fun - and yet deadly - when a place is not clearly antagonistic toward intruders/visitors but yet alien and pervaded by an intricate dynamic of which the newcomers are aware in only confusing but tantalazing hints that mix fact and fiction. For every <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hern%C3%A1n_Cort%C3%A9s\" target=\"_blank\">Cortez</a>, a hundred <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aguirre,_the_Wrath_of_God\" target=\"_blank\">Aguirres</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1481166#post1481166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because in my personal canon the kindred aren't the 'true' or original vampires, the Strix are. Human-spirits locked away by mages at the dawn of mankind, they first tamed and then escaped their otherworld prison. The Strix can come and go relatively freely, even if few of them know how.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's neat. I'm kind of averse to neat setups or broad universal statements when it comes to setting or cosmology, but i can certainly see their more common use in Awakening and Forsaken games and the appeal with the fanbase, in general and their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1481166#post1481166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred here are the result of Strix using Synthesis back in the ancient times, and this created far more than eight types of vampire. But most of them got killed, either by humans or Strix, before having any descendants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing, heard a lot of Synthesis, but never ever used any of the mechanics for the Strix in either Night Horrors: Wicked Dead, Strix Chronicle or 2e in my games up to present. Not that i have something against the Birds, quite the contrary in fact. But i mess around with images, themes and other things - clans have come and gone, created or extinguished by other beings through ways sometimes all too similar to those of the Strix, sometimes completely unrelated.<br /> <br /> Smoky serpents filled with the poison of immortality, ghosts of one's own face in a cracked mirror will take a soul and leave the corpse still walking, cats the color of the darkest night with moonlit eyes will sit in a person's chest, take their last gasp and leave emptiness &amp; undying hunger in its place. The Chronicles of Darkness are full of tales of mysterious horror, with patterns all too common but never the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-27-2023, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T14:01:36-07:00","id":1481198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1481166#post1481166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I like the idea of the vampire otherworld being the realm of the Strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that take specifically is only in the sense that it cuts story possibilities instead of creating them. Your take on the Strix's realm is fine, but if that's all, then all you have is an otherworld with no story opportunity for the vast majority of games.<br /> <br /> While it isn't a problem if you don't like the idea of exploring other worlds, the idea here is to imagine what kind of otherworldly landscapes and alien entities Vampires could deal with that resonate with the splat specifically, like all the others have,<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be a problem for there to be two answers, one practical and one inaccessible but rooted in Lore. Mage already works like that, while the Supernal is the otherworld that defines Mages, their personal exploration space is the Astral as far as it goes. Likewise you can keep this idea about the realm of the Strix and still work around the existence of something else that serves as an extra-planar or supernatural space for Vampires to get actively involved with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T19:25:59-07:00","id":1481423,"title":"","content":"I use the land of Nod for that purpouse as an otherworld who was abandoned after a natural disaster \u00bfAre vampire aliens? or something that could happen to any living being","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 05-18-2022, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T14:08:38-07:00","id":1481482,"title":"","content":"Personally I think giving vampires an otherworld where they\u2019re safe from humans would undermine the game unless there were dangers there that made it perhaps more dangerous than the real world. The Masquerade is a major theme for Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T15:09:29-07:00","id":1481486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1481482#post1481482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think giving vampires an otherworld where they\u2019re safe from humans would undermine the game unless there were dangers there that made it perhaps more dangerous than the real world. The Masquerade is a major theme for Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense, but seems like you are looking at the subject from too binary a perspective, imho.<br /> <br /> Think of the Hedge for Changelings or the Shadow for Uratha, Astral Realms for Awakened, places that can be sources of respite, wonder &amp; power and full of mystery, danger &amp; alieness <b>both</b>, with its own peculiar set of rules and logic that might be understood to a degree but not exactly simple to master or control because of it, quite the contrary in fact depending on the dynamics of its idiossyncratic natives with visitors, exiles or among themselves.<br /> <br /> Even more so with places of a nature as cracked, fractured and contradicting as the kindred that eventually attempt to find treasures to loot or a niche to fill in such mysterious abodes, found, made or other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-19-2022, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T17:42:27-07:00","id":1481498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1481486#post1481486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of the Hedge for Changelings or the Shadow for Uratha,</div> </div> </div> </div>Bad comparison, because both of these are relationships where the player splat can theoretically eke out a living indefinitely without ever dealing with people and the main reason vampires deal with people is specifically that combination of &quot;they need the context to maintain their self-control and social graces to whatever diminishing degree they still can&quot; and &quot;you are what you eat.&quot; Werewolves can sustain themselves until death on hunting spirits in the Shadow and changelings can live in the Hedge for the rest of their days as long as they make peace with being Delusional and needing a roommate or the right kind of entitlement, but if you leave a vampire alone in another dimension for long enough they will cease to be a playable character unless they take a low-set bane and sleep off the torpor of giving up Touchstones (and even then, they will be extremely susceptible to frenzy).<br /> <br /> Vampires in Requiem are people who are struggling to stay people while the unholy power in their stolen blood warps them toward being a means of stealing more blood, and an entire wing of the cosmology that doesn't have people in it to hold up that delicate contextualizing process is a distraction most ardently pursued by the inhuman and the extremely well-off. The street-level games neonates play and even the city-level games ancillae play have bills to pay and mouths to feed, and so do most of the things they're bringing into the world.<br /> <br /> Having a Kindred-specific equivalent of drilling for red-oil in the Underworld or harvesting blood-fruit in the Hedge or hunting the essence of parasite-kings in the Shadow is the kind of thing you bring into a setting as a local complication, not a ground-level concern that any given vampire might worry about when they can just hide out in &quot;mundane&quot; inaccessible places like the vents of an apartment building or under the water at a port or in somebody's basement or bedroom closet. The vampire ecology is rooted in the mortal world, and their needing to occupy space there is one more way it drives the pursuit of Havens and Feeding Grounds as means of safety and sustenance.<br /> <br /> ChroD has enough of a problem with people overlooking the supernatural's interface with the mundane world without sectioning off one of the most mundanely-connected varieties of supernatural creature away from the need to maintain that interface to play Annihilation, especially for a splat that is a bunch of different creatures just similar enough to share game mechanics through convergent evolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T23:58:42-07:00","id":1481517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1481482#post1481482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think giving vampires an otherworld where they\u2019re safe from humans would undermine the game unless there were dangers there that made it perhaps more dangerous than the real world. The Masquerade is a major theme for Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no need for this otherworld to be a place safe from humans. Actually it rarely is.<br /> <br /> While I understand <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>'s point that in many games those otherworlds work for the benefit of overlooking the interface with the mundane if the game group so desires, which I don't see as necessarily a problem, but I get where it may harm the themes, it doesn't mean that they have to even in those other games.<br /> <br /> My idea of the &quot;vampiric otherworld&quot; being a <i>twisting</i> of whatever environment they stay in for long accounts for that, but even a full blown distinct plane of existence doesn't have to be a place that safeguards vampires. Does this place has natural sources of Vitae? What happens in it during the day? Does it even exists by day? How can humans cross into it? How can vampires be brought to and from it, by their will or against it? What happens to a vampire's physiology in this place? What if torpor creeps in more easily, staying there bringing the risk of a long slumber in the wrong time? What horrors lurk there that can threaten Kindred that stay too long?<br /> <br /> You not only can answer such questions in a way that makes it interesting to explore, but unfeasible to stay too long and completely drop the human world, you can actually chose answers that make a stable grounding in the mundane world all the more necessary for any explorer to get back in one piece and in time for dinner.<br /> <br /> One example of such ruling is in cWoD's Changeling the Dreaming, if you set aside the dials defaulting to a safer exploration. Exploring the Dreaming is wonderful and nurturing to the Changelings, but staying there too long causes Bedlam. You slowly gets crazier and crazier until you become a <i>thing</i> of madness, a Lost One, and Lost Ones are effectively unplayable, partly because of how crippling their madness is, part because they become tied to a single location. And the way to avoid or recover from Bedlam is precisely by staying sufficiently grounded to your mundane life, working, paying the bills, creating something without magic that humans can appreciate. Just an example.<br /> <br /> If Kindred leave behind a sign of their passing both in and out, so when they travel to this place mortals can follow through, and when they leave the things that lurk there can come out? Maybe those things can't interact with mortals, so hunters have an edge in this place where the vampires are the prey, and back in the mundane world the Kindred need to mingle into society to lose eventual pursuers. Maybe staying there simply requires so much mundane resources that vampires cannot prepare an expedition without a solid foothold and steady supplies. Maybe it simply doesn't exist as a single continuity in space and time, but as bubbles that form and expire, risking to leave undead explorers back in the mortal world unprotected in a bad situation if they cross the limit.<br /> <br /> As you make rules for this otherworld you can make it an alternative for playing in the mundane world, or something that reinforces even more some themes as it makes even the characters that achieved to isolate themselves anyway to have an interest in going back to contact with society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T06:14:36-07:00","id":1481529,"title":"","content":"Damnation City (and the Nos clan book) treated the underground as a sort of vampire otherworld, if we\u2019re going to try to make one my first question would be what more do we need and can we just add it to the underground?<br /> There\u2019s also The Children of the Thorns from Danae Macabre. Honestly I think out of the way places where kindred might feel safe but mortals can accidentally act or intrude upon would work best for requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T14:01:52-07:00","id":1483069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1481529#post1481529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damnation City (and the Nos clan book) treated the underground as a sort of vampire otherworld, if we\u2019re going to try to make one my first question would be what more do we need and can we just add it to the underground?<br /> There\u2019s also The Children of the Thorns from Danae Macabre. Honestly I think out of the way places where kindred might feel safe but mortals can accidentally act or intrude upon would work best for requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, the Children of the Thorns and some mix up with the earlier version of Bloody Mary presented in Mythologies was one of the elements i tinkered with considerably in hashing out my own peculiar almost-cosmic things and conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}